01:03:38.840 --> 01:03:41.840
<v Derenda Hancock>This should be fun. Yeah. [LAUGHS]
<v Derenda Hancock>这应该会很有趣。是的。[笑]

01:03:41.840 --> 01:03:49.610
<v Maisie Crow>For the Pink House, which had for so long been uncloseable, this is what closing looks like, a fight.
<v Maisie Crow>对于这间长期以来无法关闭的粉红小屋来说，这就是关闭的样子，一场斗争。

01:03:49.610 --> 01:04:01.730
<v Brooke>When you check out, the receptionist is going to give you this slip of paper. It's your appointment reminder slip. It has your return date, return time--
<v Brooke>当你结账时，接待员会给你这张纸条。这是你的预约提醒单。它有你的归期，归还时间——

01:04:01.730 --> 01:04:11.900
<v Maisie Crow>For the rest of the day, patients are shown into treatment rooms as usual. A doctor does the counseling session the state mandates with patients who come in for an abortion.
<v Maisie Crow>剩下的时间里，患者像往常一样被带进治疗室。医生对那些来堕胎的患者进行州政府强制要求的咨询。

01:04:11.900 --> 01:04:12.730
<v Doctor>Morning, ladies.
<v Doctor>早上好，女士们。

01:04:12.730 --> 01:04:14.330
<v Women>Morning.
<v Women>早上好。

01:04:14.330 --> 01:04:27.770
<v Doctor>Glad you guys got in here OK. I know you guys are here for an abortion. The state wants me to scare you guys and tell you there's a risk of breast cancer related to abortion. There isn't. So now I've told you. You can forget it.
<v Doctor>很高兴你们过来了。我知道你们是来堕胎的。政府想让我吓唬你们，告诉你们有与堕胎相关的乳腺癌风险。根本没有。所以我现在告诉你们了。你可以忘了它。

01:04:27.770 --> 01:04:29.060
<v Doctor>[LAUGHTER]
<v Doctor>[笑声]

01:04:29.060 --> 01:04:41.150
<v Doctor>So there's a 24-hour law in Mississippi in terms of waiting. I can't offer you anything today. I guess you're aware the Supreme Court overturned Roe versus Wade. So this clinic will be closing down very shortly.
<v Doctor>所以密西西比州关于等待有24小时法律。我今天没法提供任何东西。我想你们知道最高法院推翻了罗诉韦德案。所以这家诊所很快就会关闭。

01:04:41.150 --> 01:06:31.900
<v Doctor>I can take care of you guys tomorrow. So if you're having the pill treatment, do not waste any time. Come back tomorrow, OK? If you need surgery, check with the front desk. They'll tell you what your options are, OK? Any questions, ladies?
<v Doctor>我可以明天照顾你们。所以如果你接受药丸治疗，不要浪费任何时间。明天再来，好吗？如果你需要手术，向接待处核实。她们会告诉你们有什么选择，好吗？有问题吗，女士们？

01:06:31.900 --> 01:06:40.910
<v Ira Glass>Nikki Lane singing a cover of "When My Morning Comes Around," which she recorded for us. Our program was produced today by Zoe Chace and Alix Spiegel and edited by Laura Starecheski.
<v Ira Glass>妮基·莱恩翻唱了《当我的早晨到来时》，那是她为我们录制的。我们今天的节目由佐伊·查斯和阿利克斯·斯皮格尔制作，劳拉·斯塔雷切斯基编辑。

